$$
\begin{aligned}
E&=\frac{\sin\left(\frac{7 \pi}{8}\right)}{\sec\left(\frac{7 \pi}{8}\right)}\\&=\sin\left(\frac{7 \pi}{8}\right)\cos\left(\frac{7 \pi}{8}\right)\\&=\frac{1}{2}\,\sin\left(\frac{7 \pi}{4}\right)
\end{aligned}
$$
The terminal sine is $\sin\left(\frac{7 \pi}{4}\right)=- \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}$.
Therefore,
$$
\begin{aligned}
E&=\frac{1}{2}\,\left(- \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}\right)\\&=- \frac{\sqrt{2}}{4}.
\end{aligned}
$$

